_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 8
---
order: 8
---
short_label: V.8
---
statement: Of unequal magnitudes, the greater has to the same a greater ratio than the less has; and the same has to the less a greater ratio than it has to the greater.
---
proof:

Let *AB* and *C* be unequal magnitudes, and let *AB* be greater, and let *D* be another, arbitrary, magnitude.

I say that *AB* has to *D* a greater ratio than *C* has to *D,* and *D* has to *C* a greater ratio than it has to *AB.*

